1
00:03:35,625 --> 00:03:41,625
Prepare for a taste of adventure.

2
00:07:11,250 --> 00:07:17,250
Charlie and the Chocolate Factory is a adventure,
comedy, family film directed by Tim Burton.

3
00:10:46,875 --> 00:10:52,875
A young boy wins a tour through the most magnificent chocolate factory in
the world, led by the world's most unusual candy maker.

4
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:28,500
Willy Wonka, played by Johnny Depp.

5
00:17:58,125 --> 00:18:04,125
Charlie Bucket, played by Freddie Highmore.

6
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:39,750
Grandpa Joe, played by David Kelly.

7
00:25:09,375 --> 00:25:15,375
Mrs. Bucket, played by Helena Bonham Carter.

8
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:51,000
Mr. Bucket, played by Noah Taylor.

9
00:32:20,625 --> 00:32:26,625
Mrs. Beauregarde, played by Missi Pyle.

10
00:35:56,250 --> 00:36:02,250
Charlie and the Chocolate Factory is a 2005 musical fantasy film directed by Tim Burton and written
by John August, based on the 1964 children's novel of the same name by Roald Dahl.

11
00:39:31,875 --> 00:39:37,875
The film stars Johnny Depp as Willy Wonka and Freddie Highmore as Charlie Bucket, alongside David Kelly,
Helena Bonham Carter, Noah Taylor, Missi Pyle, James Fox, Deep Roy, and Christopher Lee.

12
00:43:07,500 --> 00:43:13,500
The storyline follows Charlie as he wins a contest along with four other
children and is led by Wonka on a tour of his chocolate factory.

13
00:46:43,125 --> 00:46:49,125
Development for a second adaptation of Charlie and the Chocolate
Factory began in 1991, which resulted in Warner Bros.

14
00:50:18,750 --> 00:50:24,750
providing the Dahl estate with total artistic control.

15
00:53:54,375 --> 00:54:00,375
Prior to Burton's involvement, multiple directors and actors were either in
discussion with or considered by the studio to play Wonka.

16
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
Burton immediately brought regular collaborators Depp and Danny Elfman aboard.

17
01:01:05,625 --> 01:01:11,625
Charlie and the Chocolate Factory represents the first musical film directed by Burton and the first time since The
Nightmare Before Christmas that Elfman contributed to a film score using written songs and his vocals.

18
01:04:41,250 --> 01:04:47,250
Filming took place from June to December 2004 at
Pinewood Studios in the United Kingdom.

19
01:08:16,875 --> 01:08:22,875
Inspired by the book's emphasis on texture, Burton primarily used built sets and
practical effects rather than computer-generated environments.

20
01:11:52,500 --> 01:11:58,500
Wonka's Chocolate Room was constructed on the 007 Stage at Pinewood,
complete with a faux chocolate waterfall and river.

21
01:15:28,125 --> 01:15:34,125
Squirrels were trained from birth for Veruca Salt's elimination from the tour.

22
01:19:03,750 --> 01:19:09,750
Actor Deep Roy performed each Oompa-Loompa individually
rather than one performance duplicated digitally.

23
01:22:39,375 --> 01:22:45,375
Burton shot the film simultaneously alongside the stop-motion
animated film Corpse Bride, which he also directed.

24
01:26:15,000 --> 01:26:21,000
Willy Wonka-themed chocolate bars were sold, and a Golden Ticket contest
was launched as part of the film's marketing campaign.

25
01:29:50,625 --> 01:29:56,625
Early plans to promote the film with a Broadway
theatre musical were not realized.

26
01:33:26,250 --> 01:33:32,250
Charlie and the Chocolate Factory premiered on July 10, 2005, and was released in the United States on July
15 to positive critical reviews, which commended it for its visual appeal and dark tone.

27
01:37:01,875 --> 01:37:07,875
It was a box office success, grossing US$475 million and becoming
the eighth-highest-grossing film worldwide in 2005.

28
01:40:37,500 --> 01:40:43,500
The film received a nomination for Best Costume Design at the 78th Academy Awards, while Depp
was nominated for the Golden Globe Award for Best Actor – Musical or Comedy.

29
01:44:13,125 --> 01:44:19,125
It remains Tim Burton's second-highest-grossing film to date.

30
01:47:48,750 --> 01:47:54,750
The film explores themes of factory worker, london, england,
based on novel or book, chocolate, candy.

31
01:51:24,375 --> 01:51:30,375
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
